From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0210: blueline idle cores power down with PSCI CPU_SUSPEND
 (bluecpu_idle=1, off by default)

cpu_idle calls blue_idle_enter() in place of WFI: if the next timer is at
least bluecpu_idle_us (2000) away, the core's deadline goes into the
memory-mapped timer frame 0 (0x17ca0000) and the core calls CPU_SUSPEND
(power_state bluecpu_idle_ps, 0x40000003 as Linux sdm845.dtsi's CPU
power-down; entry sweet_secondary_entry). It wakes through XNU's
resume_idle_cpu -> arm_init_idle_cpu path, where blue_idle_resumed()
restores the GIC CPU interface (pe_init_fiq) and the timer deadline. The
frame's interrupt IPIs each powered-down core whose deadline has passed.
See osfmk/arm64/blueline_idle.c.

